../../core/src/edit.rs-199-//! | `set_media_color` | A video media's Camera Log (spec §11 GR-16): `color` is `{log, gamut}` (a built-in curve, its gamut defaulting to the curve's first) or `{lut}` (a `lut` media as the input conversion), converted at step 0 for every clip of the media; `null` clears it. A PQ file's `peak` (spec §11 HD-12, 1–10000 cd/m²) is the override of the peak import read into `pq`, beside either or alone; a PQ still (spec §11 HD-20 (b)) takes `peak` alone. `color` replaces the Camera Log and the override together, and `null` clears both, keeping import's reading. Refused, each in its own sentence: an audio or LUT media, and an image unless the colour is a PQ still's `peak` alone; neither or both of `log` and `lut` (and no `peak`); a `gamut` without `log` or outside the curve's pairings; a `lut` that names no `lut` media; `detected` and `pq`, which import writes; a `peak` outside 1–10000 or on media that is not a PQ file. `media_color.rs` holds the rules. |
../../core/src/edit.rs-200-//! | `set_media_speech` | A media's speech spans (format 29, spec §11 AU-110, AU-111): `spans` is `[start, end]` pairs in forward-file SOURCE ticks, stored as `media.speech` and read by every clip of the media whose `audio.duck.mode` is `speech`. An empty list is a media with no speech found, stored as such; spans equal to the stored ones are an identity. Refused, each in its own sentence: a media without audio; a span starting before 0, ending at or before its start, or ending past the media's `duration`; spans unsorted or overlapping (touching is allowed); more than 100,000. `Err` for an unknown media. `media_speech.rs` holds the rules. |
../../core/src/edit.rs-201-//! | `set_media_cursor` | A media's cursor file (road map "creator-jobs" CU5, spec §11 CU-50): `cursor` is `{path, bookmark?, in_picture}`, the `media.cursor` record of spec §5.2a, stored as given; `null` clears it, and `null` on a media with none or a value equal to the stored one is an identity. `cursor` is read strictly: neither an object nor `null`, a key other than the three, and a value the record's shape refuses (`in_picture` is required) are each an `Err` naming it, as is an unknown media. Refused, each in its own sentence: an empty path; a media that is not a video with a picture. The core opens no file and makes no `movie_size` check; the app's tool and the Media tab's Locate… do (CU-50 (b)). Consolidate's second copy and the open-time re-anchor write through it (CU-51, CU-52). `media_cursor.rs` holds the rules. |
